{"name":"Toad","hex":"#748d70","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toad","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An amphibian, a kind of frog (broad sense, order Anura) with shorter hindlegs and a drier, wartier skin, many in family Bufonidae.","A contemptible or unpleasant person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To expel (a user) permanently from a MUD or similar system, so that their account is deleted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toad","blocks":[{"text":"Toad is a generic common name for certain groups of frogs, especially those of the family Bufonidae, that are characterized by short legs and dry, leathery skin with large bumps made of the parotoid glands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg/330px-Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toad","wikidata":"Q6453151"},{"title":"Toad (Mario)","blocks":[{"text":"Toad, known in Japanese as Kinopio , is a character and race created by Japanese video game designer Shigeru Miyamoto for Nintendo's Mario franchise. A prominent red Toad serves as one of Princess Peach's handlers and appears consistently as a supporting character in the franchise."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Toad_by_Shigehisa_Nakaue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toad_(Mario)","wikidata":"Q1061603"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dong_Ho_painting_-_Nhan_nghia.jpg/330px-Dong_Ho_painting_-_Nhan_nghia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Dong_Ho_painting_-_Nhan_nghia.jpg/330px-Dong_Ho_painting_-_Nhan_nghia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe